From 16a8293207a125a3a8ea11a0b5575af98c8bfc98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:09:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tester: Add an rtems-test BSP configuration for riscv/mbv

The riscv/mbv BSP boots on QEMU's amd-microblaze-v-generic machine, which
takes its image through a loader device rather than -kernel, so
bsp_qemu_image_type and bsp_qemu_image_path are overridden rather than
using the qemu.cfg defaults.  arch is riscv32 so that qemu-system-riscv32
is selected; the RTEMS architecture directory is riscv.

Note that the machine does not terminate QEMU when RTEMS shuts down, so
every test runs until the tester's timeout and a test that fails and shuts
down is reported the same as one that hangs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tester/rtems/testing/bsps/mbv_qemu.ini | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tester/rtems/testing/bsps/mbv_qemu.ini

diff --git a/tester/rtems/testing/bsps/mbv_qemu.ini b/tester/rtems/testing/bsps/mbv_qemu.ini
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0dd1f83
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tester/rtems/testing/bsps/mbv_qemu.ini
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
